@prefix : <http://proethica.org/ontology/cases#> .
@prefix proeth-cases: <http://proethica.org/ontology/cases#> .
@prefix proeth: <http://proethica.org/ontology/intermediate#> .
@prefix proeth-core: <http://proethica.org/ontology/core#> .
@prefix iao: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_> .
@prefix dc: <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .

# Ontology Declaration

<http://proethica.org/ontology/cases> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "ProEthica Cases Ontology"@en ;
    dc:creator "ProEthica AI"@en ;
    dc:date "2026-07-10"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:comment "Case-analysis ontology: the typing vocabulary for the Step-4 analysis layer of committed ProEthica case ontologies. Eight pairwise-disjoint classes of analysis record (ethical questions and conclusions, decision points, question emergence rationales, resolution patterns, causal normative links, code provision references, and precedent case references), each an IAO information content entity about the case analysis and thereby outside the nine disjoint core categories of participants in the professional situation. Also carries the relationship properties of the analysis layer (answersQuestion, extendsQuestion) and its controlled vocabularies (citation treatment, precedent relationship, board outcome, question type)."@en ;
    owl:versionInfo "3.5.0"^^xsd:string ;
    owl:imports <http://proethica.org/ontology/intermediate> ;
    skos:changeNote "v3.0.0 (2026-07-04): slimmed to the load-bearing surface, removing the unused LangExtract-era vocabulary (case type hierarchy, decision options, argumentation structures, section templates, scoring properties; roughly 30 classes and all 38 properties, none instantiated in any committed case or referenced by any code path). Kept EthicalQuestion, EthicalConclusion, DecisionPoint (359 typed individuals corpus-wide). Added QuestionEmergence, ResolutionPattern, CausalNormativeLink, CodeProvisionReference, PrecedentCaseReference so the commit bridge can type the Step-4 phase-2 analysis individuals it previously emitted as bare owl:NamedIndividual. The removed vocabulary is recoverable from version 2.0.0 in the OntServe version history."@en ;
    skos:changeNote "v3.1.0 (2026-07-09): added the citation-treatment vocabulary. citationType datatype property on PrecedentCaseReference plus a SKOS concept scheme defining the four treatment terms (supporting, distinguishing, analogizing, overruling), each with its correspondence to the treatment-signal convention of legal citator services (Shepard's). Previously the terms existed only in the extraction prompt; the extractor's vocabulary block is kept in sync with these definitions by a unit test in ProEthica."@en ;
    skos:changeNote "v3.2.0 (2026-07-09): header cleanup (the version-removal narrative moved from rdfs:comment into the v3.0.0 change note where it belongs) and an AllDisjointClasses axiom over the eight analysis-record classes. The disjointness was verified against all 15 gold-corpus case ontologies (zero dual-typed individuals) before assertion; it makes cross-category typing errors in the analysis layer reasoner-visible instead of silently absorbed. EthicalQuestion's definition no longer calls a question a 'decision point': DecisionPoint is a sibling disjoint class."@en ;
    skos:changeNote "v3.3.0 (2026-07-09): added the PrecedentRelationshipScheme, the second controlled vocabulary of the precedent layer. The CitationTreatmentScheme classifies BOARD-AUTHORED citations by their treatment of the cited case; the PrecedentRelationshipScheme classifies SIMILARITY-DISCOVERED case relationships computed by the precedent discovery service (supporting, distinguishing, analogous, contrasting). Corresponding concepts across the two schemes are linked with skos:closeMatch; contrasting has no citation counterpart (a board does not cite a case in order to reach the opposite outcome on comparable facts). The discovery service's vocabulary block (RELATIONSHIP_TYPES in precedent_discovery_service.py) is kept in sync by the same ProEthica unit test that guards the citation treatments."@en ;
    skos:changeNote "v3.4.0 (2026-07-09): added the BoardOutcomeScheme, the outcome-polarity vocabulary behind the similarity system's outcome-alignment feature and 'same outcome' indicator (ethical, unethical, mixed, unclear). OUTCOME_TYPES in case_feature_extractor.py is kept in sync by the same ProEthica unit test."@en ;
    skos:changeNote "v3.5.0 (2026-07-10): the Q&C relationship layer becomes SPARQL-traversable (plan proethica/.claude/plans/qc-rdf-edges.md). Two object properties: answersQuestion (EthicalConclusion to the EthicalQuestion it resolves; previously the proeth:answersQuestion integer-as-string literal) and extendsQuestion (an analytical EthicalQuestion to the board EthicalQuestion it was generated from; previously the proeth:sourceQuestion integer literal, which never reached a committed graph). Both follow the edge-primary convention (CMT-3): the commit bridge emits the edge only, and the 15 gold case ontologies were converted by deterministic backfill from the committed literals. Also added the QuestionTypeScheme, the question-type vocabulary of the Q&C layer (board_explicit, implicit, principle_tension, theoretical, counterfactual); QUESTION_TYPES in question_analyzer.py is kept in sync by the same ProEthica unit test."@en .

###############################################################
# Analysis-layer classes
###############################################################

# Ethical Question and Conclusion entities
proeth-cases:EthicalQuestion a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf iao:0000030 ;  # IAO:information content entity
    rdfs:label "Ethical Question"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Specific ethical question posed in a case requiring professional resolution"@en ;
    skos:definition "An information content entity representing a specific ethical question or dilemma posed in a professional ethics case that requires systematic analysis and resolution through professional judgment"@en ;
    dcterms:source <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.artint.2022.103705> ;
    skos:changeNote "v3.2.0 (2026-07-09): 'or decision point' removed from the definition; DecisionPoint is a sibling class and the two are now asserted disjoint."@en .

proeth-cases:EthicalConclusion a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf iao:0000030 ;  # IAO:information content entity
    rdfs:label "Ethical Conclusion"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Resolution or answer to an ethical question in a case"@en ;
    skos:definition "An information content entity representing the resolution, answer, or professional decision made in response to an ethical question, grounded in professional principles and precedential reasoning"@en ;
    dcterms:source <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.artint.2022.103705> .

# Decision Point: Critical juncture requiring ethical choice
proeth-cases:DecisionPoint a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf iao:0000030 ;  # IAO:information content entity
    rdfs:label "Decision Point"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "A point in an ethics case where a professional actor must make a choice between ethically significant alternatives."@en ;
    skos:definition "Decision points mark critical junctures in ethics cases where actors face choices between alternatives with ethical implications. Per Hobbs and Moore (2005) scenario-directed decision analysis, these points structure the ethical problem space and enable systematic analysis of options, constraints, and outcomes."@en ;
    dcterms:source <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1539-6924.2005.00634.x> ;
    skos:changeNote "v2.4.2: Added to cases namespace. 845 case instances reference proeth-cases:DecisionPoint but the class was previously only defined in intermediate namespace (intermediate#DecisionPoint)."@en ;
    skos:changeNote "v3.0.1 (2026-07-04): re-anchored from proeth-core:Event to IAO information content entity. The committed individuals are composed Step-4 analysis records (identifier, decision question, options, role) with no temporal participation, and the audited core Event definition (v2.10) restricts Event to NON-volitional occurrences, which a choice juncture is definitionally not. The juncture's temporal reality is carried by the Step-3 Action/Event timeline; the DecisionPoint record is the analytic artifact marking it, uniform with the rest of the analysis layer."@en .

# Supporting analysis artifacts (added v3.0.0). Each is an information content
# entity ABOUT the case analysis, deliberately outside the nine disjoint core
# categories: an emergence rationale or a citation node is a statement about
# the analysis, not a participant in the professional situation.

proeth-cases:QuestionEmergence a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf iao:0000030 ;  # IAO:information content entity
    rdfs:label "Question Emergence"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The grounding rationale for an ethical question: which case facts, states, and tensions give rise to it."@en ;
    skos:definition "An information content entity recording why a specific ethical question arises in a case: the configuration of facts, obligations, and states from which the question emerges. Pairs one-to-one with an EthicalQuestion and preserves the analytic chain from case content to posed question."@en ;
    skos:changeNote "v3.0.0 (2026-07-04): added; the commit bridge previously emitted these individuals untyped."@en .

proeth-cases:ResolutionPattern a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf iao:0000030 ;  # IAO:information content entity
    rdfs:label "Resolution Pattern"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The recurring pattern by which a case's ethical tension is resolved."@en ;
    skos:definition "An information content entity describing the pattern through which an ethical tension or question is resolved in a case: which consideration prevailed, under what contextual conditions, and in what recurring form. Resolution patterns are the case-level record that cross-case precedent comparison draws on."@en ;
    skos:changeNote "v3.0.0 (2026-07-04): added; the commit bridge previously emitted these individuals untyped."@en .

proeth-cases:CausalNormativeLink a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf iao:0000030 ;  # IAO:information content entity
    rdfs:label "Causal Normative Link"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "An analytic statement connecting a causal step in the case narrative to its normative significance."@en ;
    skos:definition "An information content entity linking a causal element of the case narrative (an action or event and its consequences) to the principles or obligations it engages, recording why that causal step matters normatively."@en ;
    skos:changeNote "v3.0.0 (2026-07-04): added; the commit bridge previously emitted these individuals untyped."@en .

proeth-cases:CodeProvisionReference a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf iao:0000030 ;  # IAO:information content entity
    rdfs:label "Code Provision Reference"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "A citation node for a professional code provision cited in the case analysis."@en ;
    skos:definition "An information content entity referencing a specific provision of a professional code of ethics as cited in a case analysis, carrying the provision designation and text as cited."@en ;
    skos:changeNote "v3.0.0 (2026-07-04): added; provision stub individuals were previously committed untyped."@en .

proeth-cases:PrecedentCaseReference a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf iao:0000030 ;  # IAO:information content entity
    rdfs:label "Precedent Case Reference"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "A citation node for a prior board case cited in the case analysis."@en ;
    skos:definition "An information content entity referencing a prior review-board case cited as precedent in a case analysis, carrying the cited case designation."@en ;
    skos:changeNote "v3.0.0 (2026-07-04): added; precedent citation individuals were previously committed inconsistently typed."@en ;
    skos:changeNote "v3.1.0 (2026-07-09): citationType now carries the citation-treatment term; see the CitationTreatmentScheme concepts for the term definitions."@en .

# The eight analysis-record kinds are pairwise disjoint: a question is not a
# conclusion, an emergence rationale is not a resolution pattern, a citation
# node is not a decision point. Verified against all 15 gold-corpus case
# ontologies (zero dual-typed individuals) before assertion; the axiom makes
# a commit-bridge typing error a Pellet inconsistency rather than a silent
# merge. All eight remain subclasses of IAO information content entity, so
# the disjointness is internal to the analysis layer and does not interact
# with the nine-way core category disjointness.
[] a owl:AllDisjointClasses ;
    owl:members (
        proeth-cases:EthicalQuestion
        proeth-cases:EthicalConclusion
        proeth-cases:DecisionPoint
        proeth-cases:QuestionEmergence
        proeth-cases:ResolutionPattern
        proeth-cases:CausalNormativeLink
        proeth-cases:CodeProvisionReference
        proeth-cases:PrecedentCaseReference
    ) .

###############################################################
# Q&C relationship edges (v3.5.0)
#
# The load-bearing relationships of the question-and-conclusion layer as
# object properties, following the R->P->O and defeasibility materialization
# lesson: relations are edges, never only literals. Both endpoints are
# same-graph individuals with deterministic URIs (case#Question_<n>,
# case#Conclusion_<n>), minted by the commit bridge in the same pass. The
# declared domain and range make an endpoint typing error a Pellet
# inconsistency under the eight-way analysis-layer disjointness.
###############################################################

proeth-cases:answersQuestion a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain proeth-cases:EthicalConclusion ;
    rdfs:range proeth-cases:EthicalQuestion ;
    rdfs:label "answers question"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Links an ethical conclusion to an ethical question it resolves or responds to. A conclusion may answer several questions."@en ;
    skos:definition "An object property linking an ethical conclusion to an ethical question that the conclusion resolves or responds to: a board conclusion answers the board question it rules on, and an analytical conclusion answers the analytical questions it addresses."@en ;
    skos:changeNote "v3.5.0 (2026-07-10): added; replaces the proeth:answersQuestion integer-as-string literal (edge-primary, CMT-3). The question numbers stored by extraction resolve deterministically to the same-commit Question_<n> individuals."@en .

proeth-cases:extendsQuestion a owl:ObjectProperty ,
        owl:AsymmetricProperty ,
        owl:IrreflexiveProperty ;
    rdfs:domain proeth-cases:EthicalQuestion ;
    rdfs:range proeth-cases:EthicalQuestion ;
    rdfs:label "extends question"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Links an analytical question to the board question it was generated from. The committed question numbering encodes only the category (offsets 101/201/301/401); this edge is the sole parent linkage."@en ;
    skos:definition "An object property linking a generated analytical question to the board question whose inquiry it extends, recording the source-question linkage assigned at generation. Not every analytical question extends a board question; the edge is present only when a source question was assigned."@en ;
    skos:changeNote "v3.5.0 (2026-07-10): added; replaces the proeth:sourceQuestion integer literal, which was emitted by the bridge since 2026-07-09 but never reached a committed graph. Asymmetric and irreflexive after the prevailsOver precedent: a question extending itself, or a mutual extension pair, is a data error the reasoner should surface."@en .

###############################################################
# Citation treatment vocabulary (v3.1.0)
#
# How the board USES a cited case, following the treatment-signal
# convention of legal citator services (Shepard's Citations): a citing
# reference is classified by its effect on the cited authority. The terms
# are ProEthica's own; each concept records its nearest Shepard's signal
# in an editorial note. The extraction prompt vocabulary block in
# proethica/app/routes/scenario_pipeline/step4/precedents.py
# (CITATION_TREATMENTS) must match these skos:definition strings verbatim;
# tests/unit/test_precedent_vocabulary.py enforces the correspondence.
###############################################################

proeth-cases:citationType a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain proeth-cases:PrecedentCaseReference ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:label "citation type"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The citation-treatment term for a precedent case reference: how the board's analysis uses the cited case. Values are the skos:notation literals of the CitationTreatmentScheme concepts (supporting, distinguishing, analogizing, overruling)."@en ;
    skos:changeNote "v3.1.0 (2026-07-09): added; the treatment term was previously carried only in the extraction JSON and never reached the committed graph."@en .

proeth-cases:CitationTreatmentScheme a skos:ConceptScheme ;
    rdfs:label "Citation Treatment Scheme"@en ;
    skos:definition "The controlled vocabulary of citation-treatment terms for precedent case references, classifying a citation by the use the citing analysis makes of the cited case, after the treatment-signal convention of legal citator services."@en .

proeth-cases:SupportingCitation a skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme proeth-cases:CitationTreatmentScheme ;
    skos:notation "supporting" ;
    skos:prefLabel "supporting"@en ;
    skos:definition "The Board cites the prior case as authority for the position taken in the present analysis, applying its principle to reach the same result."@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "Nearest Shepard's signal: Followed (the citing opinion relies on the cited case as controlling or persuasive precedent)."@en .

proeth-cases:DistinguishingCitation a skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme proeth-cases:CitationTreatmentScheme ;
    skos:notation "distinguishing" ;
    skos:prefLabel "distinguishing"@en ;
    skos:definition "The Board cites the prior case to show that its facts or principle do not govern the present case, explaining the material difference."@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "Nearest Shepard's signal: Distinguished (the citing opinion differentiates the cited case on its facts or law)."@en .

proeth-cases:AnalogizingCitation a skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme proeth-cases:CitationTreatmentScheme ;
    skos:notation "analogizing" ;
    skos:prefLabel "analogizing"@en ;
    skos:definition "The Board cites the prior case as a parallel fact situation and reasons from the similarity, without treating it as controlling authority."@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "Nearest Shepard's signals: Explained / Harmonized (the citing opinion reasons from the cited case without adopting it as controlling). This is the characteristic mode of case-based ethics reasoning (McLaren 2003: analogizing or distinguishing a precedent against critical facts)."@en .

proeth-cases:OverrulingCitation a skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme proeth-cases:CitationTreatmentScheme ;
    skos:notation "overruling" ;
    skos:prefLabel "overruling"@en ;
    skos:definition "The Board cites the prior case as superseded: its holding is disapproved, limited, or no longer reflects the Code as applied."@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "Nearest Shepard's signals: Overruled / Limited / Questioned (the citing opinion negatively affects the cited case's authority)."@en .

###############################################################
# Precedent relationship vocabulary (v3.3.0)
#
# The second controlled vocabulary of the precedent layer: how a
# SIMILARITY-DISCOVERED case relates to the source case, as classified by
# the precedent discovery service (live similarity panel; not committed to
# case graphs). Distinct from the CitationTreatmentScheme, which classifies
# board-authored citations. RELATIONSHIP_TYPES in
# proethica/app/services/precedent/precedent_discovery_service.py must
# match these skos:definition strings verbatim;
# tests/unit/test_precedent_vocabulary.py enforces the correspondence.
###############################################################

proeth-cases:PrecedentRelationshipScheme a skos:ConceptScheme ;
    rdfs:label "Precedent Relationship Scheme"@en ;
    skos:definition "The controlled vocabulary of relationship terms for similarity-discovered precedent candidates, classifying how a discovered case bears on the analysis of the source case. Assigned by the precedent discovery service from outcome agreement and similarity structure, in contrast to the CitationTreatmentScheme terms, which record the board's own use of a citation."@en .

proeth-cases:SupportingRelationship a skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme proeth-cases:PrecedentRelationshipScheme ;
    skos:notation "supporting" ;
    skos:prefLabel "supporting"@en ;
    skos:definition "The discovered case reaches the same outcome on comparable facts, reinforcing the analysis of the source case."@en ;
    skos:closeMatch proeth-cases:SupportingCitation .

proeth-cases:DistinguishingRelationship a skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme proeth-cases:PrecedentRelationshipScheme ;
    skos:notation "distinguishing" ;
    skos:prefLabel "distinguishing"@en ;
    skos:definition "The discovered case is comparable in subject but differs in a material fact or principle, so its holding does not transfer to the source case."@en ;
    skos:closeMatch proeth-cases:DistinguishingCitation .

proeth-cases:AnalogousRelationship a skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme proeth-cases:PrecedentRelationshipScheme ;
    skos:notation "analogous" ;
    skos:prefLabel "analogous"@en ;
    skos:definition "The discovered case presents a parallel fact situation useful for reasoning by analogy, without outcome agreement being established."@en ;
    skos:closeMatch proeth-cases:AnalogizingCitation .

proeth-cases:ContrastingRelationship a skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme proeth-cases:PrecedentRelationshipScheme ;
    skos:notation "contrasting" ;
    skos:prefLabel "contrasting"@en ;
    skos:definition "The discovered case reaches a different outcome on comparable facts, marking a boundary of the principle at work in the source case."@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "No citation-treatment counterpart: a board does not cite a case in order to reach the opposite outcome on comparable facts; outcome divergence is a product of similarity discovery."@en .

###############################################################
# Board outcome vocabulary (v3.4.0)
#
# The outcome-polarity classification of a case's board conclusion,
# extracted at ingestion (case_feature_extractor.extract_outcome) and used
# by the similarity system's outcome-alignment feature. 'Same outcome'
# (the outcome_match indicator on similar-case displays) means the two
# cases carry the SAME POLARITY classification from this scheme; it does
# not assert that the specific holdings agree. Outcome alignment scores
# 1.0 for an identical classification, 0.0 for the ethical/unethical
# opposition, and 0.5 for any pairing involving mixed or unclear (the
# ternary indicator of the ICCBR 2026 evaluation). OUTCOME_TYPES in
# proethica/app/services/precedent/case_feature_extractor.py must match
# these skos:definition strings verbatim;
# tests/unit/test_precedent_vocabulary.py enforces the correspondence.
###############################################################

proeth-cases:BoardOutcomeScheme a skos:ConceptScheme ;
    rdfs:label "Board Outcome Scheme"@en ;
    skos:definition "The controlled vocabulary of outcome-polarity classifications for a review-board conclusion, characterizing whether the board held the conduct at issue ethical, unethical, both in part, or left the polarity unclassifiable. The classification summarizes the polarity of the holding over the case as a whole and is the basis of the similarity system's outcome-alignment feature."@en .

proeth-cases:EthicalOutcome a skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme proeth-cases:BoardOutcomeScheme ;
    skos:notation "ethical" ;
    skos:prefLabel "ethical"@en ;
    skos:definition "The board concluded the conduct at issue was ethical: the conclusion affirms conformance with the code, or the absence of a violation, and records no violation finding."@en .

proeth-cases:UnethicalOutcome a skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme proeth-cases:BoardOutcomeScheme ;
    skos:notation "unethical" ;
    skos:prefLabel "unethical"@en ;
    skos:definition "The board concluded the conduct at issue was unethical: the conclusion records a violation of the code, or a finding of improper conduct, and no affirmation of conformance."@en .

proeth-cases:MixedOutcome a skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme proeth-cases:BoardOutcomeScheme ;
    skos:notation "mixed" ;
    skos:prefLabel "mixed"@en ;
    skos:definition "The conclusion carries both a conformance finding and a violation finding, typically across distinct questions or aspects of the conduct."@en .

proeth-cases:UnclearOutcome a skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme proeth-cases:BoardOutcomeScheme ;
    skos:notation "unclear" ;
    skos:prefLabel "unclear"@en ;
    skos:definition "The conclusion text yields no clear conformance or violation finding; the outcome polarity is not classified."@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "Two unclear cases currently score 1.0 outcome alignment (identical classification), although agreement between two unclassified outcomes is vacuous; registered as a calibration item, corpus impact minimal (1 of 119 cases)."@en .

###############################################################
# Question type vocabulary (v3.5.0)
#
# The question-type classification of an EthicalQuestion, carried on the
# committed individual as the proeth:questionType literal. One term for the
# Board's own questions, four for the generated analytical categories. The
# committed question number encodes the category by offset (board questions
# numbered from 1, implicit from 101, principle_tension from 201, theoretical
# from 301, counterfactual from 401); the offsets are category codes, NOT
# parent references, and the parent linkage of an analytical question is the
# extendsQuestion edge. QUESTION_TYPES in
# proethica/app/services/step4_synthesis/question_analyzer.py must match
# these skos:definition strings verbatim;
# tests/unit/test_precedent_vocabulary.py enforces the correspondence.
###############################################################

proeth-cases:QuestionTypeScheme a skos:ConceptScheme ;
    rdfs:label "Question Type Scheme"@en ;
    skos:definition "The controlled vocabulary of question-type terms for ethical questions, distinguishing the questions the Board of Ethical Review itself posed from the four categories of analytical question generated to extend the board's inquiry."@en .

proeth-cases:BoardExplicitQuestionType a skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme proeth-cases:QuestionTypeScheme ;
    skos:notation "board_explicit" ;
    skos:prefLabel "board explicit"@en ;
    skos:definition "A question the Board of Ethical Review itself posed in the case record, taken from the Questions section of the case (parsed directly when possible, otherwise extracted)."@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "Committed question numbering: board questions are numbered from 1 in case order."@en .

proeth-cases:ImplicitQuestionType a skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme proeth-cases:QuestionTypeScheme ;
    skos:notation "implicit" ;
    skos:prefLabel "implicit"@en ;
    skos:definition "An analytical question the case raises but the Board did not explicitly ask, surfaced from the case facts and extracted entities."@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "Committed question numbering: implicit questions are numbered from 101. The offset is a category code, not a parent reference."@en .

proeth-cases:PrincipleTensionQuestionType a skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme proeth-cases:QuestionTypeScheme ;
    skos:notation "principle_tension" ;
    skos:prefLabel "principle tension"@en ;
    skos:definition "An analytical question identifying a conflict between extracted principles or asking how such a conflict is to be balanced in the case."@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "Committed question numbering: principle-tension questions are numbered from 201. The offset is a category code, not a parent reference."@en .

proeth-cases:TheoreticalQuestionType a skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme proeth-cases:QuestionTypeScheme ;
    skos:notation "theoretical" ;
    skos:prefLabel "theoretical"@en ;
    skos:definition "An analytical question reframing the case in the terms of an ethical theory (deontological, consequentialist, or virtue-ethical), carrying its framework designation."@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "Committed question numbering: theoretical questions are numbered from 301. The offset is a category code, not a parent reference. The framework designation rides the proeth:ethicalFramework literal."@en .

proeth-cases:CounterfactualQuestionType a skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme proeth-cases:QuestionTypeScheme ;
    skos:notation "counterfactual" ;
    skos:prefLabel "counterfactual"@en ;
    skos:definition "An analytical question whose antecedent negates or alters a fact the case asserts, testing whether a specific board conclusion would still hold under the altered fact."@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "Committed question numbering: counterfactual questions are numbered from 401. The offset is a category code, not a parent reference."@en .
